.nh
.TH "PB-PORT-FRONT-DESK" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-port-front-desk - Show or set where unnamed addresses of a machine go


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb port front-desk <machine> [<port> [http|https]] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
A machine's front desk is the port where <name>\&.<machine>\&.<domain> goes when no
port has that name: a reverse proxy such as Coolify, Traefik or Caddy. The default is
port 80 over http. Machine managers set it; the scheme defaults to https for port 443.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for front-desk

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb port front-desk homelab
  pb port front-desk homelab 443 https
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-port(1)\fP
